======================================================================
PenguinHarness (Agent runtime and web)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The Agent layer of RunHive is built on PenguinHarness, an open-source
multi-agent application platform, integrated under the Apache License 2.0.
Upstream: https://github.com/Prism-Shadow/penguin-harness
The copy integrated with this project corresponds to PenguinHarness
v0.2.13 with RunHive-specific adaptations (branding, navigation, RunOS
integration). PenguinHarness itself carries a THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES file
that remains authoritative for its own bundled components.
License text: licenses/Apache-2.0.txt

======================================================================
OSTrack / PyTracking lineage (object-tracking library)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
services/runos-api includes, under its lmm/tracking/_vendor directory, a
vendored copy of the OSTrack visual object tracking library
(https://github.com/botaoye/OSTrack), which is distributed by its authors
under the MIT License. Parts of that library's training and testing
framework derive from PyTracking (https://github.com/visionml/pytracking),
which is distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.0.
This vendored directory is a third-party component: it is distributed
with its upstream attribution and is NOT relicensed under this project's
MIT License. See the README inside that directory for the per-component
notes before redistributing it.

======================================================================
timm interface reimplementation
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The tracking module contains a small, independently written substitute
for a subset of the timm (PyTorch Image Models) API surface
(https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models, Apache License 2.0,
Copyright Ross Wightman). It implements compatible interfaces for the
functions the tracking code needs; it is not a copy of timm code.

======================================================================
ThinkPHP and BuildAdmin (PHP backend framework)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The PHP backend is built on the ThinkPHP framework and the BuildAdmin
admin scaffold, both distributed under the Apache License 2.0
(ThinkPHP: https://github.com/top-think/think ;
BuildAdmin: https://github.com/build-admin/BuildAdmin).
Framework code is pulled in as Composer dependencies and is not vendored
into this repository; the installer controller shipped by the framework
is likewise provided by the upstream packages. Business controllers and
RunHive-specific modules in services/php are original RunHive code under
the MIT License.
License text: licenses/Apache-2.0.txt

